#=GF RN [2]
#=GF RM 11142379
#=GF RT Ribosomal binding to the internal ribosomal entry site of classical swine
#=GF RT fever virus.
#=GF RA Kolupaeva VG, Pestova TV, Hellen CU
#=GF RL RNA 2000;6:1791-1807.
#=GF CC This family represents the internal ribosome entry site (IRES) of the the
#=GF CC aphthoviruses. IRES elements allow cap and end-independent translation of
#=GF CC mRNA in the host cell. The IRES achieves this by mediating the internal
#=GF CC initiation of translation by recruiting a ribosomal 43S pre-initiation
#=GF CC complex directly to the initiation codon and eliminates the requirement
#=GF CC for eIF4F [2].
#=GF WK Aphthovirus_internal_ribosome_entry_site_(IRES)
#=GF SQ 92

